  "description": "NITFUS crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H120 Cu4 Gd4 N8 O42. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 2 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 3 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Cu1A (Cu) has 2 O neighbors; Cu2A (Cu) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.295-4.547 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.71-138.86°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C56H120N8Cu4Gd4O42. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 12 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
